# Top-level Fleet ignore for the SuperDARN repo.
#
# Fleet only bundles the directory tree under each fleet.yaml. The active
# fleet.yaml for this repo lives in helm/rst-workbench/fleet.yaml, so Fleet
# normally never sees the paths below. This file is a safety net: if anyone
# adds a second fleet.yaml at the repo root or restructures the bundle, these
# patterns keep the GitRepo well under Rancher's 3 MB API request limit by
# excluding the large submodules, build outputs, datasets and notebooks.

# Submodules — every byte of RST source (57 MB after the SuperDARN merge),
# weatherlearn checkpoints, chord-dht, etc. lives here. None of it belongs
# in a Helm bundle, and a recurse-submodule git clone in Fleet can blow
# straight through the 3 MiB Rancher API request limit if these aren't
# excluded explicitly.
external/
external/rst/
src/
src/weatherlearn/
src/chorddht/
src/rl_forecast/

# Build artefacts and data
build/
val_vis/
images/
tests/
docs/

# Anything outside the helm/ tree is irrelevant to the bundle and just adds
# bytes Rancher has to base64-encode into the Bundle CR.
LICENSE
README.md
pyproject.toml
.gitmodules

# Notebooks, models, archives
*.ipynb
*.pdf
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.zip
*.h5
*.pt
*.pth
*.ckpt
*.npy
*.npz
*.mat
*.fits
*.nc
*.hdf5

# Editor / VCS
.git/
.github/
.vscode/
.idea/
.claude/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store
